@* Half its old height and no border of its own — the footer element in
   MainLayout already draws one, so this was painting a second line under it.
   It carries one short fact, and a status bar should cost the content as
   little room as it can. *@
<div class="app-statusbar">
    @* "Status: Ready" and "Active Workspace: None" were removed 2026-08-19 — both were
       hardcoded literals with no state behind them; nothing in the app ever set either,
       and a dashboard of many workspace cards has no single "active" one to report. The
       nav bar's "Online" dot had the same problem and got a real replacement instead —
       see NavMenu.razor.cs and the DevToolbox Decisions.md entry for the same date. *@
    @* Was the literal "0.1.0", which had been wrong for months — there was no version property in
       the repo at all, so nothing could have kept it right. Now from Directory.Build.props via
       AppVersion. *@
    <span class="app-statusbar-label">Version:</span>
    <span class="app-statusbar-value" title="Package version @AppVersion.Package">@AppVersion.Display</span>
    @if (AppVersion.ChannelLabel is string channel)
    {
        <span class="app-statusbar-channel"
              title="Pre-release build — expect bugs, and please report them">@channel</span>
    }
</div>

